from pathlib import Path
import json,pandas as pd
D=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;r=json.loads((D/'results.json').read_text());s=pd.read_csv(D/'source_summary.csv');profiles=json.loads((D/'profile_transfer.json').read_text());ctx=json.loads((D/'three_bit_contexts.json').read_text())
t=['# Frozen Mixed encoder: 6,000 new documents','', '## Design and verification','', 'Sample500 per original component (12 components, nine sources): four TweetEval tasks independently plus PHEME, Climate Migration, AG News,20 Newsgroups,FakeNewsNet,IRA,Airline,GoEmotions. Seed20261030, without replacement. Exclude all normalized text hashes present in the original111000 documents; also exclude identical256-token model inputs and cross-component duplicates. Normalization for duplicate detection: HTML unescape, UnicodeNFKC, casefold, whitespace. Encoder preprocessing itself is unchanged. Near-duplicate passages have not been exhaustively removed. AGNews uses its current127600-row source pool; originalMixed used an earlier extraction.','', 'Original Qwen checkpoint copied to the analysis directory; original files remain unchanged. Offline Qwen0.6B, last-token pooling, max_length256, bf16 backbone/fp32 head, K16,A6, threshold0.5, MPS, batch16. No training.64 reference control texts reproduce all1024 saved bits exactly. Original input/checkpoint hashes recorded in design.json. Twelve fixed random reference texts per active bit were archived before sampling the new documents. Original ten profile definitions were frozen in the previous analysis.','', '## Coverage and activation rates','',f"{r['known_profile_documents']}/6000 ({r['known_profile_pct']:.2f}%) new documents have a previously observed complete profile. There are{r['new_distinct_profiles']} distinct new-sample profiles;{r['previously_unobserved_distinct_profiles']} were not seen in fitting. The6000 texts average{r['mean_active']:.3f} active bits. The ten previously described profiles cover{r['top10_documents']} documents ({r['top10_documents']/60:.2f}%).",'', '| Component | n | Mean active | Previously observed profile (%) | Mean absolute bit-rate change (pp) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in s.itertuples():t.append(f'|{x.component}|{x.n}|{x.mean_active:.2f}|{x.seen_profile_pct:.1f}|{x.mean_absolute_activation_change_pp:.2f}|')
t+=['', 'Activation differences compare P(bit=1|component), not raw source mixtures. Average absolute difference across192 bit/component combinations is1.335pp; largest7.175pp. These are descriptive sample discrepancies, not predictive accuracy or proof of semantic invariance. bit_annotation_transfer.csv also reweights the fit component priors to the predetermined new sample allocation before comparing source/type compositions.', '', '## Previously interpreted exact profiles','', '| Profile | New documents | New sources | Attribute among source-eligible docs: fit -> new |','|---|---:|---|---|']
for x in profiles:
 a=''
 if 'attribute'in x:a=f"{x['attribute']}: {x['fit_attribute_positive']}/{x['fit_attribute_n']} ({x['fit_attribute_pct']:.2f}%) -> {x['new_attribute_positive']}/{x['new_attribute_n']} ({x['new_attribute_pct']:.2f}%)"
 t.append(f"|{x['profile_id']}|{x['new_n']}|"+'; '.join(f'{k}:{v}'for k,v in x['new_source_counts'].items())+'|'+a+'|')
t+=['', 'P01/P07 retain the negative-sentiment contrast with only bit11 differing. P02/P09 retain the migration contrast with only bit0 differing. These are probabilities within sources, not deterministic semantics. P07 has23 new Airline documents and P09 has55 Climate Migration documents; do not overstate precision.', '', 'P05 receives38 new documents:28 AGNews Sports items,2 Newsgroups hockey posts,7 TweetEval tweets,1PHEME tweet. All eight tweets were read: their content concerns running backs, basketball statistics, a hockey trade, Spurs, upcoming baseball/football games, David Wright, Michael Carrick and Kobe Bryant. This supports transfer of the previous sports reading across these sources, including a new PHEME example. Source/type labels alone are not a universal semantic taxonomy.', '', '## Three-bit contexts and a varying coordinate','', 'Exploratory extension beyond complete profiles. For each previously interpreted pair, enumerate triplets among its shared active bits, excluding the varying bit. Choose the triplet with highest reference-corpus source share, requiring coverage of at least25% of that source (tie-break: larger source support, then lexical order). Selection uses only fit-corpus source labels; encoder training does not. This extension was devised during analysis, not preregistered. Do not describe the triplet selection as label-free. Evaluate attribute proportions only within the relevant source.','', '| Source/context | Bit/state | Fit n | Fit attribute (%) | New n | New attribute (%) |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in ctx:
 if x['dataset']!='fit':continue
 y=next(z for z in ctx if z['source']==x['source']and z['state']==x['state']and z['dataset']=='new')
 t.append(f"|{x['source']}/{x['context']}|{x['varying_bit']}={x['state']}|{x['n']}|{x['attribute_pct']:.2f}|{y['n']}|{y['attribute_pct']:.2f}|")
t+=['', 'Airline context{0,10,13}:434 new documents,398Airline (91.71%); Climate Migration context{1,12,15}:550new,457ClimateMigration(83.09%). There are two/four new documents with previously unobserved complete profiles in these source-conditioned contexts. This small number is insufficient to validate interpretation specifically for novel complete profiles.','', '## Illustrative evidence and limits','', 'The contrast does not assign every document a correct label. For instance new_airline_0477 praises a flight crew and activates bit11 in P07, but new_airline_0169 complains about a credit and has the same profile. P01 new_airline_0340 complains about delays/communication, while P01 also contains neutral messages. Reference/new text examples are stored with IDs in profile_transfer_examples.csv.','', 'A new TweetEval document new_tweeteval_sentiment_0443 about David Wright receives P05, connecting it to the original sports documents (e.g.fit657 about Barry Bonds). Its active bits are5,6,7,9,11,13, with other coordinates off. This illustrates the code-to-reference-documents reading; it does not assign sports semantics individually to each of those six bits.', '', '240 random qualitative IDs (20/component) were fixed during sampling. Evidence cards linking their active bits to the pre-sampled reference texts are saved in qualitative_evidence_cards.md. These cards have been generated for review; no claim is made that all240 have been manually annotated or independently validated. Semantic interpretation here rests on previously interpreted profiles, supplied labels and explicitly discussed examples. No classifier fitted in this primary analysis. Future classifier comparisons are optional and separate.', '', '## Artifacts','', 'prepare.py, analyze.py, contexts.py; design.json, sampling.json, encoding_verification.json, results.json; new_documents_encoded_with_labels.csv; source_summary.csv; activation_transfer.csv; bit_annotation_transfer.csv; profile_transfer.json; three_bit_contexts.json; fixed qualitative IDs and evidence cards.']
